# Architecture

Make architecture predictable and boring. Optimize for new-developer onboarding.

## Folder structure (feature-based)

```
src/
├── api/               # Generic API client, queryClient, error envelope
├── app/               # Expo Router routes only — thin screens
├── components/ui/     # Reusable UI primitives (Button, Input, …)
├── constants/         # Magic-string-free constants & event names
├── features/<name>/   # Per-feature module
│   ├── api/           # endpoint wrappers + error parser
│   ├── components/    # feature-specific components
│   ├── hooks/         # useMutation/useQuery wrappers
│   ├── store/         # Zustand state slice
│   └── types/         # wire-level types
├── hooks/             # Cross-feature hooks
├── i18n/              # locales + i18next bootstrap
├── services/          # Storage, deviceId, analytics, logger
├── theme/             # Tokens + ThemeProvider
└── utils/             # Pure helpers (no React, no I/O)
```

## Module rules

- Separate UI, domain, and data layers strictly.
- Use absolute imports via `@/` alias for app modules.
- Prefer one concern per file; split when a file outgrows ~150 lines.
- Avoid circular dependencies. If two files need each other, extract the shared bit.
- Use DTOs to map API shapes to domain models — never pass wire types to UI.
- Centralize route names (`src/constants/routes.ts`) and permission logic.
- Use feature flags for controlled rollouts.

## File naming

- File names: kebab-case for non-component modules (`use-send-otp.ts`).
- Component files keep React's PascalCase convention (`Button.tsx`).
- One exported component per file.
